{
  "name": "belt_by_hand",
  "description": "The whole transport ladder built the way a player builds it, laid out beside the city core so the visual run actually photographs it. Every command here is one PlayController emits from a click or a drag — {system: build} throughout — except the `insert` calls that stand in for a mine dropping ore into a crate. It contains, in order: an arm lifting coal out of a crate onto a dragged line; a nine-tile straight run; a sunken belt whose two mouths are four tiles apart with somebody else's line running between them; a sorting table splitting the flow into two crates; and, south of that, a second drag that turns a corner and delivers round it. Read off state.json: logistics.totals.belts is the number of transport lines the drags produced (a corner and a tunnel each cut one), logistics.metrics.corners_turned is 1 because exactly one drag changed direction, and the crates at (134,126), (134,127), (120,128) and (125,130) hold what came down each branch. Coordinates are for seed 7 and were read off a buildability map, not guessed. It lives here rather than in tests/scenarios/ because that folder is generated by tools/gen_scenarios.py and belongs to [P00].",
  "tags": ["reference", "logistics", "visual"],
  "seed": 7,
  "ticks": 4000,
  "sample_every": 20,
